592186437270 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c152aa95-4d94-5d9c-b5bb-30ac91e12518" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437272 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437272 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94745" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437272 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437272 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $f(x,y)=x-y,$ where $x=-s\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y=s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437272 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "00d74228-1684-517b-8b3d-a3ad6a19bdf9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437272 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/21/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =(1)(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+(-1)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440471 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186440486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440471 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186440487 #edb/ref 17592186